	(text "AQEC EC front-end test bench (simulation only; nothing here is on the board).\nMirrors hardware/ec_driver_amp.kicad_sch: same refs and values for R3-R12, C16, D2-D4;\nU201-U204 are U2 sections A-D (TL074, TI SLOJ068 macromodel in models/).\nStimulus: V1/V2 stand in for +5V and the TPS60400 -5V rail (ideal);\nV3 stands in for CD4060 Q4 (U3 pin 7, VDD +5V / VSS -5V): +/-5 V square at 1/(2.2 R2 C5)/16 = 28.4 Hz.\nR100 is the EC cell (probe) between the BNC centre (CT_EXC_OUT) and shell (CT_SENS_IN).\nJP2 closed (K = 1, Rf = R4); JP1 open, so R3 hangs off the TIA output.\nChecks: expect.toml, run by check.py."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 25.4 165.1 0)
